_Last updated: 23 October 2026. Figures re-checked against their sources on that date; the Whitespark ranking-weight change is read from the report's charts. Rewritten against current 2026 data from BrightLocal, Backlinko, Shopify, Whitespark, and Ahrefs, with sources linked throughout instead of only named._

## Local SEO Statistics 2026 (Quick Answer)

The numbers that actually move local SEO decisions in 2026:

- **42%** of people who run a local search click on a result inside the Google Maps pack (Backlinko, updated December 2025). In BrightLocal's older click study, Local Pack positions 1, 2 and 3 took **17.3%**, **12.0%** and **2.9%** of all results-page clicks when no Local Services Ads were shown (BrightLocal Local Services Ads click study, San Francisco, October 2018), a share of total clicks rather than a click-through rate
- Customers are **2.7 times** more likely to consider a business reputable if they find a complete Business Profile on Google Search and Maps (Google Business Profile Help). BrightLocal's benchmark study of GBP interactions puts the average profile at around **1,260 views** and **33 website clicks** a month, with **59 total actions** (clicks, calls, and direction requests combined) (BrightLocal Google My Business Insights Study, published July 2019, analysing September 2017 to December 2018 listing data)
- **76%** of consumers who search for "near me" visit a business within a day (Backlinko, updated December 2025)
- Businesses in the top three spots in local search results average **561 Google reviews** each (Semrush, 2025, cited by Shopify, 2026)
- Replying to reviews shows no proven direct effect on rankings. It functions as a trust factor instead: **80%** of consumers say they're likely to use a business that responds to all its reviews, and **42%** say they're unlikely to use one that never replies (BrightLocal Local Consumer Review Survey 2026, US adults, published February 2026)
- AI Overviews appeared on **68%** of local business-type queries in a Whitespark study of three US cities, averaging local, informational and hybrid queries; for pure local-intent queries the rate was about **15%** (Whitespark, May 2025, cited by Shopify, 2026). Ahrefs measured a **58%** lower click-through rate for the top-ranking page when an AI Overview is present, comparing December 2023 with December 2025 in its informational-keyword samples, up from **34.5%** in its April 2025 study (Ahrefs, February 2026); no local-specific figure has been verified

